<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia confirms Oct CPI rises 0.41 percent.</title>
<headline>Indonesia confirms Oct CPI rises 0.41 percent.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's consumer price index (CPI) rose 0.41 percent month-on-month in October against a decline of 0.04 percent in September, Information Minister Harmoko said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>He told reporters increased prices of housing, textiles and services were behind the rise.</p>
<p>			   Oct	 Sep	 Oct 95</p>
<p>    Month/month    +0.41     -0.04	 +0.64</p>
<p>    Year/year	+6.56     +6.79	 +8.40</p>
<p>CPI sectors (month/month)</p>
<p>    Food	     -0.04     -0.76</p>
<p>    Housing	  +0.52     +0.52</p>
<p>    Textiles	 +0.19     +0.31</p>
<p>    Services	 +0.98     +0.12</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
</text>
